\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Back at the studio, Chanta sat on the edge of his bed and let the silence settle. The adrenaline had long since drained away, leaving behind the familiar residue of exhaustion and a headache that pulsed like a second heartbeat. He stared at the wall for a while. The wall had nothing useful to contribute.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Slowly, the fog lifted. The previous evening reassembled itself in fragments: the restaurant, the Elvi brawl, the elevator, Sarah covered in blood. Halo dying in his arms.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo pressing something into his hand.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta\'92s fingers went to his pocket. The thumb drive was still there, slightly sticky. He turned it over in his palm. Small, black, utterly unremarkable\'97the kind of object that could contain shopping lists,  state secrets or both.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He plugged it into his tablet.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The screen flickered. A video file auto-loaded. And there was Halo\'97alive, healthy, recording himself with the self-conscious awkwardness of someone who\'92d never made a video he didn\'92t intend to delete.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
