\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93So here I am, recording a vid, hoping for the best, planning for the worst. I know this all seems very tropey, my ol\'92 mate, but if you\'92re watching this now, it probably means I\'92ve gone to meet the great Serial Killer in the Sky.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I suppose I should start with a confession. You may have suspected this all along, I dunno, but I do get a sense you\'92re smarter than you make out. Certainly your lineage would lend credence to that, but I digress. First, the confession\'85\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Right, here we go. I know we\'92ve grown to be best friends, but it didn\'92t start that way, I\'92m sorry to say. In the beginning, I was assigned to protect you, to stop\'85 well, yeah\'85 to keep you alive, brother. My true name is not Haloren Smythe, but it benefits no one to speak my real name. To be honest, I\'92m not even sure what it is anymore\'85 so many lies, Chanta, so many lies. The thing is, I\'92ve lied to you, and that\'92s about the worst thing a man could do to another man\'85 I mean, women! Women lie all the time, they have to, my old mate, to compensate for all their other weaknesses. Not like us men. We have strength of character and should always tell the truth, at least among men we trust.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93So I\'92m sorry I haven\'92t been truthful with you, but I hope you\'92ll come to understand it was my job to keep you in the dark about so many things while I kept those other dumb PAPER agents from wiping you from the face of the earth. And in case you\'92re wondering, they were the taxing carpet-lickers who blew up the Stickett Inn, just to kill you! That\'92s how demented this has all become. There were other times too when they tried to kill you, like that time at Floormart when they almost tipped a load of gym equipment straight down on you. Sure, it looked like an accident\'97Floormart customers are always dying during deliveries. Lawn Mower Week is the worst. If I hadn\'92t got to the truck driver at the last second, kicked him out of the cabin and yanked the steering wheel, you would\'92ve died under an avalanche of Kleenanjerk weightlifting sets.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta paused the video.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>His calf, which should have been broken, didn\'92t hurt anymore. He gave it an experimental squeeze. Nothing.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>People had been trying to kill him. And Halo stopped them.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He pressed play.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Like any calcified old intelligence agency, PAPER\'92s left hand never knows what testicle the right hand is scratching, or even if one department is gonna rim another department or fist it till it bleeds. We\'92re supposed to be on the same side, Chanta, but there are so many sides and so many angles to play, and an agent who doesn\'92t at least consider all the angles is a dead agent. Like that bitch Avi Grubler\'85 she nearly got you, brother, with that bomb of hers. You\'92d already left with that bitch Sarah Jacobson, just in time. I suppose I should thank her for that. But I took my eye off you for just a minute\'85 I was so hungry, brother. Your Stacy bitch made me so damn hungry, brother. She played on my appetites and she called me out, and she made me so hungry.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yeah, so that\'92s the confession. I\'92m a deep-cover PAPER agent, assigned to keep you alive. And I nearly failed you, brother, so please forgive me. Please forgive me, as the man among men you most certainly are.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93While we\'92re on the subject of Sarah Jacobson, lemme just tell you, because I love you, brother, you know I do. I never bought that she was your girlfriend. Stacies like that never go out with men like you; they have no appreciation for an honest stand-up guy like you or me. Women like her don\'92t accept the natural order of things. They\'92re underhanded and manipulative, they try to control us in dishonourable ways, ways you never see coming. The sooner we can breed men in test tubes, the sooner we can put women in their place. Farm them, I say, and when we need a new one, we just go to market and get a new one. And when we\'92re finished with them, we just sell them for pig feed. Circle of life, brother.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta stopped the video again.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>His shoulders had climbed up near his ears. He pushed them back down.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo had always been weird about women. This was just... more of that. Kinda.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He pressed play.\
